      <div>
        <h1 class="ForewordTitle">Foreword</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="foreword" id="foreword"></a>ISO (the International Organization for Standardization)
is a worldwide federation of national standards bodies (ISO member bodies). The work of preparing International Standards is normally carried out through ISO technical committees. Each member body interested in a subject for which a technical committee has been established has the right to be represented on that committee. International organizations, governmental and non-governmental, in liaison with ISO, also take part in the work. ISO collaborates closely with the International Electrotechnical Commission (IEC) on all matters of electrotechnical standardization.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ff374ced-d6ae-46f1-8afc-913f3a8d70f6" id="_ff374ced-d6ae-46f1-8afc-913f3a8d70f6"></a>The procedures used to develop this document and those intended for its further maintenance are described in the ISO/IEC Directives, Part 1. In particular the different approval criteria needed for the different types of ISO documents should be noted. This document was drafted in accordance with the editorial rules of the ISO/IEC Directives, Part 2 (see www.iso.org/directives).</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7aa9cb95-171b-4c1a-b56e-2234f1038f21" id="_7aa9cb95-171b-4c1a-b56e-2234f1038f21"></a>Attention is drawn to the possibility that some of the elements of this document may be the subject of patent rights. ISO shall not be held responsible for identifying any or all such patent rights. Details of any patent rights identified during the development of the document will be in the Introduction and/or on the ISO list of patent declarations received (see www.iso.org/patents).</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_081109bd-3799-4249-ae56-3935cd37c420" id="_081109bd-3799-4249-ae56-3935cd37c420"></a>Any trade name used in this document is information given for the convenience of users and does not constitute an endorsement.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0d6854ec-7497-4109-947a-11a335a02547" id="_0d6854ec-7497-4109-947a-11a335a02547"></a>For an explanation on the voluntary nature of standards, the meaning of ISO specific terms and expressions related to conformity assessment, as well as information about ISO&#x2019;s adherence to the World Trade Organization (WTO) principles in the Technical Barriers to Trade (TBT) see the following URL: www.iso.org/iso/foreword.html.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b230938e-0b42-44fb-9158-45147c57bcbb" id="_b230938e-0b42-44fb-9158-45147c57bcbb"></a>This document was prepared by Technical Committee ISO/TC 37, <i>Language and terminology</i>, Subcommittee 4, <i>Language resource management</i>,
Work Group 4, <i>Lexical Resources</i>.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_5c0d2675-38c9-42e0-b7ec-e4343fa2f67c" id="_5c0d2675-38c9-42e0-b7ec-e4343fa2f67c"></a>This is the first edition of this document.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="MsoNormal">
        <br clear="all" style="mso-special-character:line-break;page-break-before:always"/>
      </p>
      <div class="Section3"><a name="introduction" id="introduction"></a>
        <h1 class="IntroTitle">Introduction</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1a93c926-d4c5-4291-a680-95b471e6ac21" id="_1a93c926-d4c5-4291-a680-95b471e6ac21"></a>Personal names are among the most commonly exchanged information on the
Internet.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_022cd48c-2f01-45eb-ade9-1931859d05a3" id="_022cd48c-2f01-45eb-ade9-1931859d05a3"></a>This International Standard facilitates the interchange and interaction
of names between humans and applications without loss of fidelity.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="MsoNormal">&#xA0;</p>
    </div>
    <p class="MsoNormal">
      <br clear="all" class="section"/>
    </p>
    <div class="WordSection3">
      <p class="zzSTDTitle1">Computer applications in terminology&#xA0;&#x2014; Naming&#xA0;&#x2014; Structure of personal names</p>
      <div><a name="_scope" id="_scope"></a>
        <h1>1<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Scope</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d8cba50b-45cd-4155-9e4a-bd4e873eff8b" id="_d8cba50b-45cd-4155-9e4a-bd4e873eff8b"></a>This document specifies the &#x201C;personal name&#x201D; data model,
suitable for the machine encoding of personal names, for
digital storage and transmission of the following data elements:</p>
        
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    personal name components,
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    cultural name profiles for personal name patterns,
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo1;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    template for displaying personal names.
  </p>

        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_38e093e1-39f5-4e1e-b9a5-8fcc9d507978" id="_38e093e1-39f5-4e1e-b9a5-8fcc9d507978"></a>This document does not handle the linkage of a personal name to an identity.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8598970c-7227-4dba-abb1-8b89093e29cb" id="_8598970c-7227-4dba-abb1-8b89093e29cb"></a>The personal name model is used to encode a person&#x2019;s personal names for:</p>
        
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo2;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    as a static data element
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo2;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    as an interoperable data structure used with databases
  </p>

        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_06e807d2-062f-48cf-a6c1-2558f49da1fd" id="_06e807d2-062f-48cf-a6c1-2558f49da1fd"></a>The cultural name profile model is used to guide rendering of a name model instance as a string
as appropriate to the applied cultural name profile.</p>
        <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2df15602-076a-43c8-a670-78c339c6a4be" id="_2df15602-076a-43c8-a670-78c339c6a4be"></a>The usage of this personal name model also applies to the following business cases:</p>
        
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    bibliographic management
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    business cards (such as vCard)
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    personal identification documents
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    electronic messaging, e-commerce
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    travel industry
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo3;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    postal
  </p>

      </div>
      <div>
        <h1>2<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Normative references</h1>
        <p class="MsoNormal">The following documents are referred to in the text in such a way that some or all of their content constitutes requirements of this document. For dated references, only the edition cited applies. For undated references, the latest edition of the referenced document (including any amendments) applies.</p>
        <p class="NormRef"><a name="ISO639-1" id="ISO639-1"></a>ISO 639-1, <i> Codes for the representation of names of languages&#x2009;&#x2014;&#x2009;Part 1: Alpha-2 code</i></p>
        <p class="NormRef"><a name="ISO15924" id="ISO15924"></a>ISO 15924, <i> Information and documentation&#x2009;&#x2014;&#x2009;Codes for the representation of names of scripts</i></p>
      </div>
      <div><a name="terms" id="terms"></a><h1>3<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Terms and definitions</h1><p class="MsoNormal">For the purposes of this document,
    the following terms and definitions apply.</p>
<div class="Note"><p class="Note">???: </p></div><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-name" id="term-name"></a>3.1</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">name</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7ba440dd-2b95-4329-a351-35aaa0758fb9" id="_7ba440dd-2b95-4329-a351-35aaa0758fb9"></a>verbal <i>designation</i> (<a href="#ISO5127">ISO 5127:2017, 3.1.5.24</a>) of an <i>individual concept</i> (<a href="#ISO5127">ISO 5127:2017, 3.1.2.16</a>)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO5127">ISO 5127:2017, 3.1.5.28</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-person" id="term-person"></a>3.2</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">person</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_f8f05ed6-a289-4903-87bd-cad0787d4214" id="_f8f05ed6-a289-4903-87bd-cad0787d4214"></a>human being</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO29003">ISO/IEC TS 29003:2018, 3.12</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-personal-name" id="term-personal-name"></a>3.3</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">personal name</p>
  <p class="AltTerms" style="text-align:left;">anthroponym</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_8f3fbdf5-bf99-447f-9320-214adce5a384" id="_8f3fbdf5-bf99-447f-9320-214adce5a384"></a>name (<a href="#term-name">3.1</a>) of a <i>person</i> (<a href="#term-person">3.2</a>)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO5127">ISO 5127:2017, 3.1.5.43</a>, modified &mdash; preferred term <i>personal name</i> used in this document,
replaced term <i>human being</i> with term <i>person</i> used in this document.]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-locale" id="term-locale"></a>3.4</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">locale</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_070e145f-d8fc-418a-9910-119f5ab03c3e" id="_070e145f-d8fc-418a-9910-119f5ab03c3e"></a>definition of the subset of a user&#x2019;s environment that depends on
language and cultural conventions</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO9945">ISO/IEC/IEEE 9945:2009, 4.211</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-criterion" id="term-criterion"></a>3.5</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">criterion</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6be82cb4-c704-492c-8a9b-b99d0bde4142" id="_6be82cb4-c704-492c-8a9b-b99d0bde4142"></a>threshold or value of a variable to be met</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO14198">ISO/TS 14198:2012, 3.2</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-name-display-profile" id="term-name-display-profile"></a>3.6</p>
  <p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">name display profile</p>
  <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_4a8c5d2a-f78a-4d3e-8d1e-71716a1412a7" id="_4a8c5d2a-f78a-4d3e-8d1e-71716a1412a7"></a>profile that associates a set of <i>criteria</i>
(<a href="#term-criterion">3.5</a>) and <i>layout templates</i> (<a href="#term-name-display-template">3.12</a>)</p>
<p class="TermNum"><a name="term-data-type" id="term-data-type"></a>3.7</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">data type</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1fc03148-1d16-42d8-9e10-1ec9f101f6cb" id="_1fc03148-1d16-42d8-9e10-1ec9f101f6cb"></a>set of representable values</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO9075-1">ISO/IEC 9075-1:2016, 3.1.1.4</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-primitive-type" id="term-primitive-type"></a>3.8</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">primitive type</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_7e00fa06-2155-4ba7-9fe5-80282205353b" id="_7e00fa06-2155-4ba7-9fe5-80282205353b"></a>pre-defined basic datatype without any substructure, such as an integer or a
string</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO14813-5">ISO 14813-5:2010, B.1.118</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-localized-string" id="term-localized-string"></a>3.9</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">localized string</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_df3eaa96-3a83-43b0-911c-0d1fd243d8e2" id="_df3eaa96-3a83-43b0-911c-0d1fd243d8e2"></a>user-context-dependent string determined by a particular <i>locale</i> (<a href="#term-locale">3.4</a>)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO20944-1">ISO/IEC 20944-1:2013, 3.21.10.2</a>, modified &mdash; added reference to term <i>locale</i>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-template-fragment" id="term-template-fragment"></a>3.10</p>
  <p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">template fragment</p>
  <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_627e52ec-0076-4e00-bd19-de846a5277be" id="_627e52ec-0076-4e00-bd19-de846a5277be"></a><i>localized string</i> (<a href="#term-localized-string">3.9</a>)
or <i>name component</i> (<a href="#term-name-component">3.11</a>)
used in a <i>name display template</i> (<a href="#term-name-display-template">3.12</a>)</p>
<p class="TermNum"><a name="term-name-component" id="term-name-component"></a>3.11</p>
  <p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">name component</p>
  <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ae77237f-31b7-4793-b3dd-9448b47a826d" id="_ae77237f-31b7-4793-b3dd-9448b47a826d"></a>component that forms part of a <i>personal name</i> (<a href="#term-personal-name">3.3</a>)</p>
<p class="TermNum"><a name="term-name-display-template" id="term-name-display-template"></a>3.12</p>
  <p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">name display template</p>
  <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_bf0341dd-5101-4f5a-bafc-6ece9c46cbbf" id="_bf0341dd-5101-4f5a-bafc-6ece9c46cbbf"></a>specification of ordering of
<i>template fragments</i> (<a href="#term-template-fragment">3.10</a>)
for a <i>name display profile</i> (<a href="#term-name-display-profile">3.6</a>)
of a <i>cultural name display profile</i> (<a href="#term-cultural-name-display-profile">3.13</a>)</p>
<p class="TermNum"><a name="term-cultural-name-display-profile" id="term-cultural-name-display-profile"></a>3.13</p>
  <p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">cultural name display profile</p>
  <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_21b7231b-cdb0-445d-a5bd-c9268a7feb77" id="_21b7231b-cdb0-445d-a5bd-c9268a7feb77"></a>set of <i>name display profiles</i> (<a href="#term-name-display-profile">3.6</a>)
pertaining to a particular <i>culture</i> (<a href="#term-culture">3.14</a>)</p>
<p class="TermNum"><a name="term-culture" id="term-culture"></a>3.14</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">culture</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_842f0d50-b8f8-4327-9f20-c8958cb4cd2d" id="_842f0d50-b8f8-4327-9f20-c8958cb4cd2d"></a>pattern of beliefs and expectations shared by the organization&#x2019;s members</p>

<div class="Note"><p class="Note">Note 1 to entry: </p></div><p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO14105">ISO/TR 14105:2011, 2.1</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-language-id" id="term-language-id"></a>3.15</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">language identifier</p>
  <p class="AltTerms" style="text-align:left;">language symbol</p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_34b99560-f46f-4d01-b4e5-f3d959fd1c95" id="_34b99560-f46f-4d01-b4e5-f3d959fd1c95"></a>symbol that uniquely identifies a particular language</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO639-3">ISO/IEC 639-3:2007, 3.3</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-script" id="term-script"></a>3.16</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">script</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_df366e18-e33c-4dd1-b4ff-f763755eff9a" id="_df366e18-e33c-4dd1-b4ff-f763755eff9a"></a>set of graphic characters used for the written form of one or more languages</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO15924">ISO 15924, 3.7</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-script-code" id="term-script-code"></a>3.17</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">script code</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_59151363-ae5d-461a-89a7-858f63b7efde" id="_59151363-ae5d-461a-89a7-858f63b7efde"></a>combination of characters used to represent the name of a <i>script</i>
(<a href="#term-script">3.16</a>)</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO15924">ISO 15924, 3.8</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="term-uri" id="term-uri"></a>3.18</p><p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">URI</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_4c06d047-216c-4f0c-a675-aac44aa4852c" id="_4c06d047-216c-4f0c-a675-aac44aa4852c"></a>compact sequence of characters that identifies an abstract or physical resource</p>
<p class="MsoNormal">[SOURCE: <a href="#ISO12234-3">ISO 12234-3:2016, 3.4</a>]</p><p class="TermNum"><a name="_style" id="_style"></a>3.19</p>
  <p class="Terms" style="text-align:left;">style</p>
  <p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b0a733ab-53d6-4f8f-818a-264da0fc2ebc" id="_b0a733ab-53d6-4f8f-818a-264da0fc2ebc"></a>TODO.</p>
